================================================================================

Project Name: BudgetBasics
Theme: NextGen BudgetBee
Category: Web Innovation Unleashed
Version: 1.0 (Final Release)
Author: Student Web Engineering Team

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PROJECT DESCRIPTION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
BudgetBasics is an educational web application designed as a Single Page 
Application (SPA) to teach students, interns, and young professionals personal 
finance and budgeting fundamentals. The website features interactive 50-30-20 
calculators, savings goal projections, gamified needs-vs-wants classification, 
an interactive session expense tracker with CSV export, money mistake case studies, 
an infographics learning gallery, and a rule-based AI chatbot assistant.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. MANDATORY INSTALLATION & EXECUTION INSTRUCTIONS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step 1: Extract the submitted project ZIP archive into any local folder.
Step 2: To run the project locally with full JSON dataset support:
        Method A (Using Python Web Server):
        - Open Terminal / PowerShell in the project directory.
        - Run command: python -m http.server 8000
        - Open your browser and navigate to: http://localhost:8000

        Method B (Using VS Code Live Server):
        - Open the project folder in Visual Studio Code.
        - Right-click index.html and select "Open with Live Server".

        Method C (Direct Browser Launch):
        - Double-click index.html in any modern browser (Chrome, Edge, Firefox, Safari).

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. LIST OF ASSUMPTIONS MADE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Assumption 1:
The application adheres strictly to the Aptech SRS "No-Backend" constraint. 
All data persistence is handled via Client-Side LocalStorage / SessionStorage, 
and pre-populated data is loaded from JSON files located in the /data directory.

Assumption 2:
Currency values can be dynamically toggled by the evaluator between PKR, USD, 
INR, EUR, and GBP. Default currency is set to PKR (Rs 35,000 allowance benchmark).

Assumption 3:
Feedback and Contact forms perform robust client-side regular expression (regex) 
validation and render interactive toast confirmations without transmitting 
sensitive data to external servers.

Assumption 4:
The AI Chatbot ("BeeBot AI") executes an in-browser NLP token & fuzzy matching 
engine against a structured JSON intent knowledge graph, guaranteeing 100% 
offline availability without third-party API dependencies.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. TEST DATASETS PROVIDED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- /data/sample_budget.json  : Pre-configured student budget benchmarks.
- /data/mistakes.json       : 6 Real-life student money mistake scenarios.
- /data/chatbot_kb.json     : NLP intent patterns and structured responses.
- /data/quiz_data.json      : Needs vs Wants items and knowledge check questions.
- /data/infographics.json   : Categorized visual guides and summary points.
- /data/quotes.json         : Curated financial motivation quotes for the ticker.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. HARDWARE & SOFTWARE REQUIREMENTS VERIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
- Hardware: Minimum 4GB RAM, Intel Core i3 or higher, modern display.
- Software: Visual Studio Code, Modern Web Browser (Google Chrome, Edge, Firefox).
- Dependencies: Bootstrap 5.3 (CDN), Chart.js (CDN), FontAwesome 6 (CDN).

